<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kullu Dussehra</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kullu">Kullu</a> Dussehra is a week-long festival held each autumn on the Dhalpur maidan at Kullu, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himachal-pradesh">Himachal Pradesh</a>, beginning on Vijayadashami. Hundreds of village deities are carried in palanquins to pay homage to Raghunath, the presiding god of the former Kullu kingdom, whose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariot</a> is drawn through the town. The festival dates from the 17th century, when Raja Jagat Singh installed the image of Raghunath at Kullu.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kullu-dussehra.jpg" alt="Kullu Dussehra" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Meerah Dhiman · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Raghunath_Ji_and_Mata_Sita.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
